@startuml auth_session_sequence
title Frontend - Auth and session sequence

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
autonumber

actor User
participant App
participant "SiteHeader / PatternPage" as Trigger
participant "AuthDialog" as Dialog
participant "usePlaygroundApp" as Hook
participant "api" as Api
database "Backend\n(cookie-based auth)" as Backend
collections "localStorage" as Storage

== Open auth modal ==

User -> Trigger : click Connexion / Inscription
Trigger -> Hook : openAuth(mode)
Hook --> App : isAuthOpen = true
App -> Dialog : render modal

== Login or register ==

User -> Dialog : submit credentials
Dialog -> Hook : handleAuthSubmit(event)
activate Hook
Hook -> Api : loginUser(payload)\nor registerUser(payload)
Api -> Backend : POST /api/auth/login or /register
Backend --> Api : AuthResponse + Set-Cookie
Api --> Hook : response.user
Hook -> Storage : persistSession(user)
Hook --> App : currentUser updated\nisAuthOpen = false
deactivate Hook

== Session restore on startup ==

App -> Hook : initial mount
activate Hook
Hook -> Storage : loadPersistedUser()
Storage --> Hook : cached user or null
alt backend connected
  Hook -> Api : getCurrentUser()
  alt access cookie still valid
    Api -> Backend : GET /api/auth/me
    Backend --> Api : current user
    Api --> Hook : user
  else access expired
    Hook -> Api : refreshUserSession()
    Api -> Backend : POST /api/auth/refresh
    Backend --> Api : AuthResponse + rotated cookies
    Api --> Hook : response.user
  end
  Hook -> Storage : persistSession(user)
else backend fallback
  Hook -> Hook : keep local UI session only
end
Hook --> App : currentUser settled
deactivate Hook

== Logout ==

User -> Trigger : click Deconnexion
Trigger -> Hook : handleLogout()
activate Hook
Hook -> Api : logoutUser()
Api -> Backend : POST /api/auth/logout
Backend --> Api : 204 + clear cookies
Hook -> Storage : clearPersistedSession()
Hook --> App : currentUser = null
deactivate Hook

note right of Hook
Le frontend ne manipule jamais
les cookies HttpOnly directement.
Il s appuie sur fetch + credentials: include.
end note

@enduml
